12. The High Court has held the following five circumstances as proved:
(1) That Mahendra Singh visited Jodhpur on 9th January, 1954;
(2) That he took on rent a house belonging to Manohar Singh;
(3) That 13 air tickets were purchased through him for 13 different persons from Karachi to London.

(4) That he had a talk on telephone from Jodhpur with Raj Sachdev for the cancellation of four tickets; and 

(5) That the endorsement between A and B on all the passports was in the handwriting of the appellant.
